{
  "version": "pressure-digest/1",
  "about": "Inputs (ShadowInputs JSON, as `acpmux machine verdict` reads them) and the pressure_digest each must give, in cmux (cmux-host-budget pressure_digest.rs) and leo-workspace (tools/shadow_admission.py pressure_digest). The canonical text: one compact JSON object, keys sorted: host (trimmed, up to its first dot, ASCII lowercased, always), cores (when over 0), load1, psi_cpu_some_avg10, available_fraction, swap_growth_mb_per_min (when finite), mem_pressure (when set and not unknown), swap_used_fraction (used/total clamped to 0..1, when total is over 0). Non-integers are written with three decimals (half to even on the exact binary value), trailing zeros and point dropped, -0 as 0. Left out: now_ms, health_at_ms, previous, ram_total_bytes, sessions, new_session. Hash: FNV-1a 64 over the UTF-8 text, written fnv1a64: and 16 hex digits. The same file is in both repositories; change both together.",
